  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nThe issue is:\n```html\nlocation.hash = \"#1\";\ndocument.open();\n```\nwill make there be an onging navigate event, but fragment navigations don't set ongoing navigation. So the check in [#document-open-steps](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#document-open-steps:~:text=If%20document%27s%20node%20navigable%20is%20non%2Dnull%20and%20document%27s%20node%20navigable%27s%20ongoing%20navigation%20is%20a%20navigation%20ID%2C%20then%20stop%20loading%20document%27s%20node%20navigable%2E) won't call `stop`, which would abort ongoing navigations.\n\nThe fix would be to call [#inform-the-navigation-api-about-aborting-navigation](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#inform-the-navigation-api-about-aborting-navigation) if the ongoing navigation isn't a `NavigationID`",
